<p>A small Embraer EMB-721 aircraft carrying five people crashed into a residential building in the Silveira neighborhood of Belo Horizonte, Brazil, on Monday, killing three people and injuring two others, local officials and firefighters said. The plane had departed Pampulha Airport shortly after noon and was bound for São Paulo before it went down minutes later. Local reports identified the pilot as Wellington de Oliveira, 34, and one of the people who died at the scene as Fernando Moreira Souto, 36. A third victim, businessman Leonardo Berganholi, 50, died later after being taken to Hospital João XXIII.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/c-xjctIjxqfN-72k2VHhtBqt3HIttuDJtT1kuh_Yo1FkHNaXisjfNkHhXicqSbfxQAdkVEH17EOP3lB-ZnKuWPFQ02jYfqiWHBUQx2jNq6a8dxKzku8eROc52p7Xap5iSDu6IYlw4RVfDxegdlxW9LCtsKnWqQoXSf77DTMJjJOnT2SGR33Si_5VsWejxbx_MfnG9LHh8fJj1vnHeMXq2Y9n8stGMOPDqWyWU1McA-CAjuzNZ5rFk5xXM4U' alt='Avião de pequeno porte cai e atinge prédio em Belo Horizonte' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Takeoff difficulty: Reports said the pilot told Pampulha Airport’s control tower he was having difficulty during takeoff before the aircraft hit the building.</li><li>Video evidence: Footage from TV Globo showed the plane losing altitude and banking left before the collision, while other videos showed wreckage lodged in the building.</li><li>Crash investigation: Investigators from the Brazilian Air Force and other aviation authorities launched a formal inquiry into the cause, including possible mechanical or operational issues.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Minas Gerais fire department: The fire department said firefighters applied foam over spilled fuel and found no explosion risk after the crash. (<a href='https://jovempan.com.br/noticias/brasil/aviao-de-pequeno-porte-colide-com-predio-em-bh.html'>Jovem Pan</a>)</li><li>Hospital foundation in Minas Gerais: The local hospital foundation said the two surviving occupants remained hospitalized in stable condition. (<a h